{"type":"message","id":"145b14ec","parentId":"a178a5f0","timestamp":"2026-10-20T02:40:23.490Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed the bug in `ledger/currency.py`. All 5 tests pass now, including the 4 in `tests/test_totals.py`.\n\n**Cause:** `to_cents` turned prices into cents with `int(amount * 100)`. In floating point, `19.99 * 100` comes out as `1998.9999999999998`, and `int()` just drops the decimals, so you got 1998 instead of 1999. Any price that falls just below a whole cent this way lost a cent.\n\n**Fix:** `to_cents` now uses `round(amount * 100)`, which rounds to the nearest cent instead. Python's `round` sends exact halves to the even number, but prices with two decimal places never land on a half after multiplying by 100, so that doesn't matter here. Nothing else needed changing: tax and discounts already work in whole cents and round half up on their own."}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"vertex-anthropic","model":"claude-opus-5-5","usage":{"input":2,"output":280,"cacheRead":25505,"cacheWrite":2340,"totalTokens":28127,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0},"cttl":{"ephemeral5m":2340}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1792464019886,"responseId":"msg_vrtx_011CgCiUfoXjQmRGpD7Vjy5V","duration":3602.7444780000005,"ttft":3577.749166999998,"contextSnapshot":{"promptTokens":27847,"nonMessageTokens":13307}}}
